      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I meant the new crossvm can call a normal future gh ioctl to test that existence so there is no need for GH_ANDROID_TENATIVE_UAPI.\n\nI don\u0027t think we can be sure that the \"normal future gh ioctl\" will have a different number than what ACK has. For instance, if `struct gh_userspace_memory_region` changes during kernel.org review, ACK will have the older version and crosvm won\u0027t know whether it should use the android14-6.1 `struct gh_userspace_memory_region` or the final kernel.org definition.\n\n(I picked `struct gh_userspace_memory_region` as it was the first struct in include/uapi/linux/gunyah.h; no special concerns about this particular struct)",
